<http://data.silknow.org/object/db5fe374-28cf-399c-82a6-27b308cc17fd/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Stevengraph picture woven in silk and mounted on green card. The picture shows the heroine Grace Darling rowing in heavy seas, aiming to rescue nine people from a ship wrecked near Farne Island's lighthouse. She is wearing a red bodice and a blue skirt. The mount is inscribed 'Woven in pure silk' and 'Grace Darling'. On the reverse of the mount is a trade label listing other Stevengraphs printed in 1901."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/db5fe374-28cf-399c-82a6-27b308cc17fd> .

